\begindata{lset,44980607488}
\V 1
\begindata{text,44980565344}
\textdsversion{12}
The dog days of summer have a tendency to make people restless, easily 
agitated, and maybe even a little puckish. It's a prime season for scandals 
both grave and fanciful. Isaac Butler's "exhaustively investigated and 
deeply persuasive" history \htmlatk-italic{\htmlatk-link{The Perfect Moment}} 
considers the explosive reaction to a 1980s Robert Mapplethorpe art exhibit 
and the questions of censorship that continue to reverberate today. And on 
the lighter side, Alexandra Vasti's \htmlatk-italic{\htmlatk-link{Scandal 
of the Summer}} pits outspoken ladies against rakish smugglers in a Regency 
romance that features delightful banter and un petit assassination plot. 
Cooler heads do prevail, at any rate, and the well-read ones most of all!


--\htmlatk-link{Dave Wheeler}, senior editor, \htmlatk-italic{Shelf 
Awareness}


\enddata{text,44980565344}
0 0 0 44980565344 0 0 0
